-- stated assumptions (trusted, not verified; not verdicts) --
        each line below is a precondition with no read-back mechanism, so it
        carries no verdict. What the certificate asserts, it asserts ON these.
          - the configured host set is the fleet this gate is meant to measure: .keel-hosts (or $KEEL_REMOTE_HOSTS) is the only statement of that intent, so there is no second source to check it against
          - each name reaches the machine it is meant to reach: every witness of a host's identity — cpuinfo, the CPU model that enters the record, the hostname itself — is reported BY the host under test, so a name pointed at the wrong machine reports consistently about the wrong machine

